{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Vr76NEu4YNPnsgZXDpYbCt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 1: Project Context Analysis\n\nThis project derives formal specs from GNU C source, generates Go implementations via an AI orchestrator, and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU binaries.\n\n## Step 2: Project State Summary\n\n- **Problem**: Unix utilities lack implementer-level specs; re-implementations diverge on edge cases. This project formalizes behavior from C source and uses differential testing to gate generated Go code.\n- **Architecture**: `docs/` (specs) → `magefiles/` (orchestrator) → `cmd/<util>/` (generated binaries) + `pkg/` (shared libs: sys, format, testutils)\n- **Current state**: Specs complete for cat (rel01.1), sponge (rel01.2), du (rel01.3), wc (rel03.0), ls (rel04.0/04.1). Code lives only at generation-merged git tags, not on the working branch. One open issue: #295 (pkg/sys, rel00.0).\n- **Current release**: `01.1` — one use case: `rel01.1-uc001-cat`, codestatus `not started`.\n\n## Step 3: Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease `01.1` has one use case: implement `cmd/cat`. The PRD and use case are complete. No library dependencies block this — cat needs only stdlib and the bufio/os primitives. Per P2, implementation and tests must be separate tasks; with the 1-task limit, I propose the implementation task first.\n\n## Step 4: Proposed Task\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/cat concatenation and flag processing (rel01.1-uc001-cat)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd005-cat.yaml (cat PRD -- locate actual filename under docs/specs/product-requirements/ if number differs)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.1-uc001-cat.yaml (end-to-end execution path for cat)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.1.yaml (test cases the implementation must satisfy)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component responsibilities and pkg/ dependency rules)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: cat binary -- file concatenation, stdin fallback, and all flag processing\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Read files named as CLI arguments in order and write their content to stdout; when no arguments are given or '-' appears as a filename, read from stdin\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement -n (number all output lines starting at 1) and -b (number non-blank output lines starting at 1, skipping blank lines); line counters accumulate across all input sources without resetting between files\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement -s (squeeze two or more consecutive blank lines to one), -E (append literal $ before each newline), -T (render tab characters as ^I), -v (render non-printing characters using ^ and M- notation), and -A (equivalent to -vET)\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Exit 0 when all inputs are processed successfully; when a file cannot be opened or a read error occurs, write a diagnostic to stderr and continue processing remaining arguments, exiting non-zero after all arguments are processed\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"cmd/cat is a standalone binary package; it must not import other cmd/ packages\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Wrap os.Stdout in a bufio.Writer for all output to avoid per-byte syscall overhead; flush before exit\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Line number counters (-n, -b) are global across all input files -- do not reset between files -- matching GNU cat behavior\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"'go build ./cmd/cat/' succeeds and produces a binary\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"'go vet ./cmd/cat/' reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Invoked with no arguments, the binary reads from stdin and echoes each byte to stdout\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Invoked with a non-existent filename, the binary writes a message to stderr and exits non-zero without writing that file's content to stdout\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Invoked with -n across two input files, line numbers continue from the first file into the second without resetting\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19110,"cache_read_input_tokens":15967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19110},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8277499-3a5b-40f7-8bac-7fabdca3d440","uuid":"b19438c1-6ad3-4bdb-a7e5-a391a18cbe44"}
